# achieve-rows.golden - the rows BOTH ACHIEVE doors must print.
#
# The C door (sdk/c/examples/achieve) and its TypeScript twin
# (Doors/achieve/app.ts) are the same door for a caller, so for one
# fixture they must produce these strings exactly. Backlog 4.13.
# tests/test_achieve_rows.c asserts the C side; the twin is asserted by
# web/backend/tests/doors/achieve-rows-match-the-c-door.test.ts.
#
# Data: achieve-board.listing and achieve-catalog.listing, beside this.
# `wide` is an 80-column caller, `compact` a 40-column one.
#
# NOT covered, by the sysop's call of 2026-09-15 (option 3), because the
# C door cannot do them at all: the twin's profile view and account
# states, its unlocked mark on a catalogue row (this fixture is rendered
# with an empty unlocked set), its `== FAMILY ==` grouping lines and the
# leaderboard's two heading lines. Parity is on the ROWS, which is where
# a format drifts.

